                                    <watches>4</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="14233986" author="cxie" created="Thu, 4 Dec 2014 07:40:06 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The problem is when a file info is evicted from ledger cache, the bookie forgets to flush header of the file info which cause the fence bit lost.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The fix is pretty easy. Added a test case to reproduce this behavior.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14234017" author="hustlmsp" created="Thu, 4 Dec 2014 08:43:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;we also have similar fix in twitter&apos;s branch. looks like you hit the same issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;the patch looks good to me. +1. and mark the fix version to 4.4.0, 4,3.1. do we need to mark this for 4.2.* branch? &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ikelly&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ikelly&quot;&gt;ikelly&lt;/a&gt; this seems to be a critical bug, since it affects the fundamental fencing mechanism.  &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14234114" author="ikelly" created="Thu, 4 Dec 2014 10:47:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I plan to have a 4.2.4 release to push out &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-799&quot; title=&quot;Distribution schedule coverage sets don&amp;#39;t take gaps in response lists into account when writequorum &amp;gt; ackquorum&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;BOOKKEEPER-799&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;BOOKKEEPER-799&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, so we can put this in there too.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14234139" author="ikelly" created="Thu, 4 Dec 2014 11:30:17 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Committed 6a94e4 in master.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14234315" author="ikelly" created="Thu, 4 Dec 2014 16:20:01 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Actually, going to leave open until it&apos;s in all branches.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14235392" author="ikelly" created="Fri, 5 Dec 2014 11:27:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Committed b1493c to branch-4.2&lt;br/&gt;
Committed 3a6830 to branch-4.3&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15285413" author="mmerli" created="Mon, 16 May 2016 21:47:33 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Closed as part of BookKeeper-4.4.0 release&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
